\description{
Creates density plots, trace plots, and autocorrelation plots
for a given parameter of a JAGS model.
}
\details{
Indicator traces place each batch at its mean iteration index
and keep chains separate. A final switching batch with one draw has no rate
and is not drawn. The components of a publication-bias mixture are traced
with \code{parameter = "bias"}. An unavailable indicator diagnostic raises a
\code{BayesTools_plot_condition}.

The trace shows the iteration index of every retained draw on its
x axis (thinned chains keep their positions), as \code{\link[=JAGS_draw_geometry]{JAGS_draw_geometry()}}
numbers them: BayesTools iteration indices, which count the requested
adaptation also when JAGS runs no adaptation iterations and therefore can
differ from the iteration counter of JAGS.
Autocorrelation uses the retained iteration positions.
Requested lags without finite observation pairs, beyond the retained chain,
or with nonfinite autocorrelation are retained as \code{NA}. One warning per
parameter and chain has classes \code{BayesTools_autocorrelation_unavailable}
and \code{BayesTools_plot_condition}, with \code{parameter}, \code{chain},
\code{unavailable_lags}, \code{pair_count} and \code{reason} fields.
Computed x/y objects retain full-length \code{pair_count} and
\code{unavailability_reason} attributes; both renderers display finite bars
only. No iteration compression, replacement estimate or confidence band is
introduced.

Coordinates whose convergence role is \code{"structural"} (see
\code{\link[=JAGS_check_convergence]{JAGS_check_convergence()}}) are constants of the prior: the weight bins that
the prior fixes (for example by \code{\link[=wf_fixed]{wf_fixed()}}) or the coefficients of an
ordered prior with a point total and fixed allocation. The density and
autocorrelation diagnostics omit them when their draws are constant, and
when nothing else remains the call returns \code{NULL} with a message, as for
a spike prior; the trace is produced as for any other parameter. A parameter
with a \code{\link[=prior_none]{prior_none()}} prior is not sampled: the call returns \code{NULL} with
a message for every type of \code{statistic = "value"}.
}
